message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the paper below."
title: "Physics-Informed Auxiliary Critics for Behavioral Decision-Making at Unstructured Intersections"
abstract: >-
  Code, configuration and analysis outputs for a study of whether the choice of
  partial differential equation used to regularize a value function changes how
  a reinforcement-learning agent negotiates an unstructured T-intersection under
  partial observability. A recurrent PPO agent selecting among five discrete
  behavioral actions is augmented with an auxiliary critic trained on one of
  four PDE residuals (hard and soft Hamilton-Jacobi-Bellman, Eikonal
  time-of-arrival, control barrier function) and their convex fusion, evaluated
  across twelve scenario-maneuver cells at ten training runs each.
